<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sultan bin Saqr Al Qasimi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> bin Saqr <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Al Qasimi</a> was sheikh of the Qawasim of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a> and Sharjah for most of the period from 1803 to 1866. After British attacks on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras">Ras</a> al-Khaimah in 1809 and 1819 he made Sharjah the family's chief seat, and he signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-maritime-treaty-of-1820">General Maritime Treaty of 1820</a> and the later truces with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p></div>
